WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.767
The proof of production portfolio.

2
00:00:03.067 --> 00:00:07.967
What surrounds your code decides whether it reads as a tutorial or as real work.

3
00:00:09.167 --> 00:00:10.633
There are two kinds of repo.

4
00:00:10.933 --> 00:00:13.700
A side project says: I followed a tutorial.

5
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.167
A proof of production repo says: I have done this job.

6
00:00:17.467 --> 00:00:20.233
The difference is entirely in what surrounds the code.

7
00:00:21.433 --> 00:00:22.967
Here are six things to add.

8
00:00:23.267 --> 00:00:26.300
An architecture diagram at the top of the README.

9
00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:32.567
A trace link from LangSmith or Langfuse, showing multi-step execution with timings and costs.

10
00:00:32.867 --> 00:00:36.200
An eval report, with your golden set committed to the repo.

11
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:41.800
A benchmark table of latency and cost, before and after, with a reproducible method.

12
00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:47.100
A real repo structure, with source, tests, docker, workflows and typed code.

13
00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.043
And a written post-mortem.

14
00:00:49.043 --> 00:00:52.267
This is the section senior engineers actually read.

15
00:00:53.467 --> 00:00:55.078
Now quantify everything.

16
00:00:55.078 --> 00:01:02.733
Here is a real style of claim: cost per query reduced by sixty two percent, from forty one paise to sixteen paise.

17
00:01:03.933 --> 00:01:06.433
The mistake is a paragraph of adjectives.

18
00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:10.412
Instead, say the number, the method, and the quality you held.

19
00:01:10.412 --> 00:01:13.200
That single sentence outperforms the paragraph.

20
00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:17.667
But you can only write that sentence if you measured from day one.

21
00:01:17.967 --> 00:01:19.100
So measure first.

22
00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:20.500
Then optimize.

23
00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:21.712
Then prove it.

24
00:01:21.712 --> 00:01:25.033
That is why evals come before optimization, always.

25
00:01:26.233 --> 00:01:27.003
Let's recap.

26
00:01:27.003 --> 00:01:29.633
Proof of production beats a side project.

27
00:01:29.933 --> 00:01:33.800
Add a diagram, trace, evals, benchmarks and a post-mortem.

28
00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:35.533
Quantify every claim.

29
00:01:35.833 --> 00:01:38.131
And evals come before optimization.

30
00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:40.167
Next up: this week's checklist.
